# {{ repo_name }}

Bootstrapable Python project with a clean command model:

- `uv` manages environments and dependencies.
- `task <name>` runs all developer workflows and setup commands.

## Requirements
- Python {{ python_version }}+
- `uv`
- Go Task v3 as a standalone executable (validated with 3.53.1)

Install Task with `brew install go-task` on macOS or `winget install Task.Task` on Windows.
For Linux and other installation methods, see the [native installation instructions](https://taskfile.dev/docs/installation).
Install `uv` using its [installation instructions](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/).
Confirm both executables are on PATH with `task --version` and `uv --version`.

## Initialize The Repo
```bash
task repo:init
task quality:verify
```

Initialization links `agent-docs` to `~/agent-docs` if that shared directory exists.
This is one way to share Markdown files across projects without installing them as skills.
The link stays out of Git; existing entries are preserved. Run `task repo:agent-docs` to retry linking later.

## Run
```bash
task app:run
```

## Task namespaces

| Namespace | Workflows |
| --- | --- |
| `repo:*` | Dependency sync, environment setup, Git hooks, and cleanup |
| `quality:*` | Formatting, linting, types, tests, verification, and full checks |
| `security:*` | Repository and staged secret scans |
| `app:*` | Run and build the generated application |

Use `task help` to list the commands available in the current repository.
Arguments still go after `--`, for example `task quality:test -- -k "smoke or cli"`.

## Command Model
Use Task for developer workflows:

```bash
task quality:fmt
task quality:fmt:check
task quality:lint
task quality:type
task quality:test
task quality:verify
task app:run
task app:build
task repo:clean
```

Use Task for setup and the command catalog:

```bash
task help
task repo:init
task repo:hooks
```

Pass command arguments after `--`, preserving shell quotes:

```bash
task quality:test -- -k "smoke or cli"
```

Bare `task` and `task help` list the available workflows. Composite tasks run sequentially and stop on failure.

`task quality:check` runs `task quality:verify`.

## Secret Scanning

This repo includes a local Gemini API key scan for strings that match the format-aware
`AIza[A-Za-z0-9_-]{35}` pattern. Version 1 scans only Gemini-style keys, has no allowlist, and
keeps CI `gitleaks` checks as separate defense in depth.

Run a repo-wide audit of tracked files:

```bash
task security:scan
```

Install the repo-managed pre-commit hook:

```bash
task repo:hooks
```

After installation, each commit scans staged added lines only. It does not scan unchanged old
lines, full git history, or non-staged working tree changes.

## Dependencies
- Add a runtime dependency: `uv add <package>`
- Add a dev dependency: `uv add --dev <package>`
- Sync lockfile + env: `uv sync --group dev`

